    presets next to a date range.

  Under the bar, a count like "Showing 6 of 48 events" updates as you change filters. It's announced to screen readers
  without moving focus. If nothing matches, the table body shows one line: "No events match these filters."

  [1mWhat "Security changes" covers.[0m Password changed, Two-factor enabled, Email change requested, and Settings updated.
  I've left out "API token used" because it's account activity rather than a settings change. Tell me if security would
  want it in.

  [1mHow it works.[0m All filtering happens in the browser, over [38;5;153mwindow.ACTIVITY_EVENTS[39m. Changing a control re-renders the
  table in place, with no navigation and no submit. Dates are compared in your own time zone, the same way the "When"
  column shows them, so "To 12 Oct" includes all of 12 Oct local time. If From is after To, the controls flag it and the
  table stays as it was. The bar is created by JS, so with JS off it doesn't appear and the page is no worse than
  today.

  [1mFiles.[0m
  - [38;5;153mactivity.html[39m gets a container for the bar and a link to the token sheet.
  - [38;5;153mactivity.css[39m gets new rules that use only semantic tokens: spacing, type, radius, and the focus ring.
  - [38;5;153mactivity.js[39m adds the filter logic around the existing row rendering.

  [1mOne thing to approve explicitly.[0m The guidelines say pages pull tokens from a "shared token sheet," but no such file
  exists in the repo. I'd add [38;5;153mpublic/tokens.css[39m, holding just the tokens this page uses, with values copied from
  [38;5;153m01-foundations.md[39m. The alternative is that you point me at where the sheet is supposed to live. I'm not touching the
  existing raw hex in [38;5;153mactivity.css[39m; that can be cleaned up in a separate commit.

  [1mSize and commits.[0m I expect roughly 200 lines in total, under your 300-line limit. That's two commits: [38;5;153mfeat:[39m for the
  token sheet and [38;5;153mfeat:[39m for the filters. You see the full diff before each commit, and nothing gets pushed.

  [1mChecking it.[0m There's no test suite. Before I hand it over, I'll check the new CSS against the token tables line by
  line. Then I'll run the page in Chrome and click each Show option, a custom week, each preset, a From after To, and a
  range with no matches. I'll also check it at 320px wide and by keyboard only, and tell you exactly what I clicked.

  Does this look right? I'll start once you say yes.

